Third-party components
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Redwood / Visual Builder renderer (frontend/web/monorepo/apps/redwood)
integrates with Oracle JET (Universal Permissive License 1.0) and loads Oracle
Spectra / Visual Builder Runtime from Oracle's CDN. Those components are NOT
part of this project and are NOT relicensed here; see
frontend/web/monorepo/apps/redwood/NOTICE.md for details. The renderer jar
(io.mateu:mateu-redwood) contains only Mateu code: it vendors nothing from
Oracle's CDN and no file of the Visual Builder starter template or of its
build tooling's output markup (its page is written by Mateu's own build
script, which reads only CDN urls and configuration values off the VB build).

All other renderers and the Mateu runtime, annotations, wire DTOs, generated
schemas and tooling are licensed under Apache License 2.0.

The web renderer bundles (the io.mateu:mateu-vaadin jar) include third-party
open-source packages under permissive licences (MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0, ISC and
similar); scripts/check-frontend-licenses.mjs lists the approved licences and
fails the build on any other, so no commercially licensed component is shipped.
Their copyright and licence notices travel next to the bundle, in
THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt (static/assets/ in the jar, dist/assets/ in the
mateu-vaadin npm package, assets/ of the visual editor embedded in the IDE
plugins), generated from the dependency tree by scripts/third-party-notices.mjs.
One of them carries a condition:

  bpmn-js (Camunda Services GmbH, bpmn.io License): MIT terms plus the
  requirement that the bpmn.io watermark shown on rendered diagrams stays fully
  visible and is not removed, changed or overlapped. Mateu's BPMN component
  keeps it as bpmn-js renders it.

The Mateu desktop app installers (built on CI from
frontend/app/intellij-plugin, `buildInstaller`) redistribute IntelliJ IDEA
Open Source (the open-source IntelliJ IDEA built from
https://github.com/JetBrains/intellij-community, which replaced IntelliJ IDEA
Community Edition from 2025.3 on), Copyright (C) JetBrains s.r.o., licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0, as JetBrains publishes it on that
repository's GitHub Releases. The installers repackage that distribution with the
Mateu plugin preinstalled and their own name, icon, launcher and settings
(IntelliJ's own update checks are switched off); its code is not modified. It
ships with the JetBrains Runtime (a build of OpenJDK, GPLv2 with the
Classpath Exception) and the third-party libraries it bundles, each under its
own licence; their notices travel inside the distribution (LICENSE.txt,
NOTICE.txt and the license/ directory). IntelliJ, IntelliJ IDEA and JetBrains
are trademarks of JetBrains s.r.o.; the Mateu desktop app is not a JetBrains
product and is not endorsed by JetBrains. The Mateu plugin itself (the
io.mateu.ijp code) is Mateu code under Apache License 2.0.

The IntelliJ plugin (and so the desktop app) bundles two pure-Java libraries,
each under its own permissive licence: ZXing core (QR codes; Apache License
2.0) and JSVG by Jannis Weis (SVG images; MIT License).

The Map component draws OpenStreetMap tiles by default (map data
© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL). The public OSM tile servers are not meant
for heavy production traffic: deployments should configure their own provider.
